  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is essentially the azepane homolog of guanethidine, a guanidine-containing adrenergic neuron blocker known to have poor blood-brain barrier penetration. The absence of a large lipophilic group, combined with the strongly basic guanidine and azepane moieties that are protonated at physiological pH, predicts inadequate CNS access.",
